      "role": "user",
      "content": "That looks perfect. Having a specific section like 4.2 to point to will really make the argument feel grounded. \n\nOne follow-up though—I'm looking for the specific percentage ranges mentioned in that section. I want to make sure the 40% dip I'm describing isn't just \"within range,\" but actually looks relatively standard or even slightly above average for volatility compared to what they saw in the study. \n\nWhat specific stability variance percentages or standard deviations does that Journal of Biotechnology and Biochemistry paper cite for these types of engineered proteins? I'll put those numbers right next to our findings in the thesis to show the committee how normal this is.",
      "source": "evaluator"
